{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #706: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $L(r)$ be such that if $G$ is a graph formed by taking a finite set of points $P$ in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and some set $A\\subset (0,\\infty)$ of size $r$, where the vertex set is $P$ and there is an edge between two points if and only if their distance is a member of $A$, then $\\chi(G)\\leq L(r)$.\n\nEstimate $L(r)$. In particular, is it true that $L(r)\\leq r^{O(1)}$? Current best: The case $r=1$ is the Hadwiger-Nelson problem, for which it is known that $5\\leq L(1)\\leq 7$. Prize: no. Tags: chromatic number, graph theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_b90902da357eb5398a8b8d423f630ebcdd8b3bc68d1ab79c9f0d139540712b22","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:706","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_d277b1116416e9e5","object_root":"sha256:f4829e3f512c6035cead4ac42d260a6479e3d3b57a7be62937fad479322edc69","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:706"